# deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (MXFP4 MoE, 384 experts top-6, DSpark drafter), one LUMI-G
# node, through the lumi_dsv41 plugin on LAIF 20261028 (vLLM 0.26.0). Not an Aitta model:
# kept in the registry's format (models/*.env, branch exp/aitta-best-configs) so it can move
# there. Best since 2026-11-24 (README status lines; jobs below).
# Run: <these variables> sbatch repro/deepseek_v41_gfx90a/run_v4_serve.sh
MODEL=deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
NODES=1; TP=8; PP=1; DP=1   # expert parallel (--enable-expert-parallel, set by V41=1)
# Plugin switches (run_v4_serve.sh). Prefix caching is on by default for V4.1 and the
# plugin sets VLLM_PREFIX_CACHE_RETENTION_INTERVAL=4096 itself.
V41=1 AMDGCN_USE_BUFFER_OPS=0 BF16_LINEAR=1 COMPILE=1 TRITON_LOGITS=1 MHC_TRITON=1
CUSTOM_AR=1 SPARSE_DECODE=1 MOE_SMALL=1 MOE_TILES=1 DSPARK=5 PREFILL_LOGITS=1 SPARSE_PREFILL=1
# Server: run_v4_serve.sh's base (--max-model-len 32768 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.92
# --kv-cache-dtype fp8, PIECEWISE graphs, async scheduling, MRV2) plus:
VLLM_ARGS="--max-num-seqs 64 --max-num-batched-tokens 2048"
# Interactive agents: --max-num-batched-tokens 8192 halves time to first token
# (2.6 / 1.9 s at 8-16k / 16-32k against 8.6 / 4.1 s) and gives 6 % more throughput, at
# a 10-20 % higher time per output token (job 23973421, before the mHC and launch tuning).
# Throughput-bound: --max-num-seqs 128 (970 tok/s at 128 users, job 23870587).
#
# Results (natural GSM8K prompts, 1k in / up to 512 out; agentic = agentic_bench.py):
#   decode out tok/s at 1 / 16 / 32 / 64 users: 64.2 / 471.1 / 729.6 / 963.2 (job 23983327)
#   cold prefill TTFT at 4k / 16k / 30k tokens: 1.19 / 3.77 / 6.99 s (job 23984875)
#   agentic, 32 conversations at 8-30k context: 166 out tok/s, 87 % cached (job 23983987)
#   GSM8K 99 % (200), sanity 5/5, needles 2/2 (job 23983987)
STATUS=best
